<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Kalman Steel Joists Advertisement - American Builder, July 1935</title>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;0,900;1,400&family=Great+Vibes&family=Oswald:wght@500;700&display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            color: #111;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
        }

        .page-container {
            background-color: #fff;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 900px;
            padding: 40px 60px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            position: relative;
        }

        /* Header */
        .header {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            font-size: 14px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        /* Main Title */
        .main-title {
            text-align: center;
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
            font-size: 48px;
            font-weight: 900;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            margin: 10px 0 30px 0;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            /* Simulating the arch slightly with transform isn't easy without SVG, keeping it straight but large */
            transform: rotate(-2deg); /* Slight tilt to mimic the dynamic feel, though the original is arched */
        }

        .main-title span {
            display: inline-block;
        }

        /* To mimic the arch better */
        .arched-title {
            text-align: center;
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
            font-size: 52px;
            font-weight: 900;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            position: relative;
            height: 80px;
        }

        .arched-title svg {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
        }

        /* Main Illustration Placeholder */
        .main-illustration {
            width: 100%;
            height: 400px;
            background-color: #eee;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .main-illustration::after {
            content: "[Illustration: Man in suit looking at three model houses]";
            color: #666;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        /* Subheadline */
        .subhead {
            text-align: center;
            font-family: 'Great Vibes', cursive;
            font-size: 42px;
            margin: 20px 0 30px 0;
            color: #000;
        }

        /* Body Text Layout */
        .body-content {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .text-row-top {
            display: flex;
            gap: 40px;
        }

        .col-left, .col-right {
            flex: 1;
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        .text-row-bottom {
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
            align-items: flex-start;
        }

        .bottom-text-left {
            flex: 1;
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        .bottom-images {
            display: flex;
            gap: 15px;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: flex-end;
            width: 250px; /* Fixed width for images area */
        }

        .joist-img {
            width: 110px;
            height: 90px;
            background-color: #333;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: flex-end;
            color: #fff;
            font-size: 10px;
            padding-bottom: 5px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        .joist-img-placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 70px;
            background: #222;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            color: #aaa;
            font-size: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

        .joist-label {
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 11px;
            color: #000;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .bottom-text-right {
            flex: 1;
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        /* Footer */
        .footer {
            margin-top: 40px;
            text-align: center;
            border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding-top: 20px;
        }

        .footer-logo-area {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .bethlehem-logo {
            width: 60px;
            height: 70px;
            background-color: #ddd;
            border: 2px solid #000;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 10px;
            text-align: center;
            clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 100% 25%, 100% 75%, 50% 100%, 0% 75%, 0% 25%);
            background: #fff;
        }

        .footer-title {
            font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif;
            font-size: 36px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            /* Outline effect */
            -webkit-text-stroke: 1px black;
            color: white; 
            /* Fallback for outline text */
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #ccc;
            color: #fff;
            -webkit-text-stroke: 1px #000;
        }

        .footer-title-solid {
             font-family: 'Oswald', sans-serif;
             font-size: 32px;
             font-weight: 700;
             text-transform: uppercase;
             letter-spacing: 1px;
             color: #000;
             margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .footer-text {
            font-size: 11px;
            line-height: 1.4;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        p {
            margin-top: 0;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .drop-cap {
            float: left;
            font-size: 3em;
            line-height: 0.8;
            padding-right: 5px;
            padding-top: 5px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page-container">
    <div class="header">
        <span>16</span>
        <span>American Builder, July 1935.</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Arched Title Simulation -->
    <div class="arched-title">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 100" preserveAspectRatio="none">
            <text x="50%" y="80%" text-anchor="middle" font-family="'Playfair Display', serif" font-size="60" font-weight="900" fill="black" letter-spacing="5">KALMAN STEEL JOISTS</text>
        </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="main-illustration">
        <!-- Placeholder for the main drawing -->
    </div>

    <div class="subhead">bring added values to any home</div>

    <div class="body-content">
        <!-- Top Text Section (2 Columns) -->
        <div class="text-row-top">
            <div class="col-left">
                <p><span class="drop-cap">W</span>HILE fire-safety ranks first among the advantages of Kalman Steel Joists, they bring additional values that appeal to any prospective home-builder.</p>
                <p>The combination of Kalman Steel Joists with concrete floor slab and plaster makes a floor structure that, while forming an impassable barrier to fire, transmits very little sound and vibration, preventing noises overhead from disturbing occupants of rooms below. A floor structure that cannot shrink to cause cracks where walls and floor meet, and that is immune to the dreaded termite, whose ravages are spreading rapidly.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-right">
                <p>livable. They make his investment sounder, because his home—which often represents the savings of years—is less subject to swift obsolescence, will need fewer repairs.</p>
                <p>Kalman Steel Joists in no way complicate the builder's work. Often they simplify it. These joists require no cutting or fitting. They reach the site in the exact lengths needed and are quickly installed and the concrete poured.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Bottom Text Section with Images (3 Columns layout effectively) -->
        <div class="text-row-bottom">
            <div class="bottom-text-left">
                <p>These advantages, which make a difference in the building cost of only a few cents a square foot, provide the owner with a dwelling that is more</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bottom-images">
                <div>
                    <div class="joist-img">
                        <div class="joist-img-placeholder">[Diagram: Steel Joist]</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="joist-label">KALMAN JOIST</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="joist-img">
                        <div class="joist-img-placeholder">[Diagram: Steel Joist]</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="joist-label">MACMAR JOIST</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bottom-text-right">
                <p>Tell the prospective home-owner about the advantages of Kalman Steel Joists. The fact that he may have in mind a relatively small dwelling offers no obstacle to their use. Kalman Joists can be applied as economically to a six-room home as to a large, pretentious one. They are of course adaptable to any style of architecture.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
        <div class="footer-title-solid">Kalman Building Steel</div>
        <div class="footer-logo-area">
            <div class="bethlehem-logo">BETHLEHEM<br>STEEL</div>
            <div class="footer-text">
                KALMAN STEEL CORPORATION, <i>Subsidiary of Bethlehem Steel Corporation</i>. General Offices: Bethlehem, Pa. District Offices: Albany, Atlanta, Baltimore, Boston, Buffalo, Chicago, Cincinnati, Cleveland, Detroit, Houston, Milwaukee, Minneapolis, New York, Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, St. Louis, St. Paul, Syracuse, Washington. <i>Pacific Coast Distributor:</i> Pacific Coast Steel Corporation, San Francisco, Seattle, Los Angeles, Portland, Honolulu. <i>Export Distributor:</i> Bethlehem Steel Export Corporation, New York.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
